{"name":"Enviable","hex":"#53983c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"enviable","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Arousing or likely to arouse envy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enviable"}],"entries":[{"title":"Envy","blocks":[{"text":"Envy is an emotion which occurs when a person lacks another's quality, skill, achievement, or possession and either desires it or wishes that the other lacked it. Envy can also refer to the wish for another person to lack something one already possesses so as to remove the equality of possession between both parties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/The_mad_woman-Theodore_Gericault-MBA_Lyon_B825-IMG_0477.jpg/330px-The_mad_woman-Theodore_Gericault-MBA_Lyon_B825-IMG_0477.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Envy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg/330px-Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg/330px-Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Invidia, allegorical painting by Giotto di Bondone, c. 1305–1306","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Invidia%29.jpg/500px-Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Invidia%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Invidia%29.jpg/500px-Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Invidia%29.jpg?utm_source=en.